<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 75,298 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 75,298 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 75,298 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday compared to 75,332 tonnes in the same period on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Wednesday   October 29</p>
<p>    Export cargo		30,465	18,773</p>
<p>    Import cargo		44,833	66,559</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, four ships sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, two were expected to sail and seven were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Crude oil		67,603	 Johar		  30/10</p>
<p>Gas oil		  42,000	 Crystal River	31/10</p>
<p>High speed diesel    52,000	 Al - Maqwa	   31/10</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     31,802	 Cargo Explorer	1/11</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
